metadata
    Title : Door State Machine
    Author : Leon Starr
    Document ID : mint.elevator3.td.7
    Modification date : April 30, 2026
    Version : 3.4.4
    Organization : Model Integration, LLC
    Copyright notice > MIT
    Organization logo > mint
domain Elevator Management
class Door
interaction events
    Door opened
    Passenger open
    Passenger close
    Time to close
    Hold released
    Door closed
    Lock
    Unlock
    Door blocked
completion events
    Open delay canceled
    Keep trying
    Cannot close door
--
state OPENING
activity
transitions
    Door opened > OPEN
    Passenger close > CLOSING
ignore
    Passenger open
        The passenger can hit the open button all they like at this point,
        but it will be ignored since the door is, in fact, opening now.
    Lock
        <Lock checked later> There’s nothing to do at this point, but we assume the lock attribute
        will be set and we will check it later, so the event info is not lost.
    Hold released
        <Release checked elsewhere> This condition is saved as the Hold attribute status and
        checked in the HOLDING OPEN state.
can't happen
    Door closed
        Door is opening, so it should not detect ‘closed’.
    Door blocked
        Block can only be reported while closing the door. (door jams while opening are
        not modeled, in this release anyway)
    Unlock
        <Cabin not moving> Cabin is not able to progress to a state where it can send this event while we are
        opening the door.
    Time to close
        <Delay always canceled> This is a delayed event that is canceled on any path that enters the current state.
--
state OPEN
activity
    my Bank .= /R4/R2/R1/Bank
    Blocked? delay = my Bank.Block clear time :
        delay = my Bank.Passenger load time
    Time to close -> me @delay
transitions
    Passenger close > Cancel open delay
    Time to close > HOLDING OPEN
ignore
    Passenger open
        <Already open so ignored> Door is already open, so this is ignored.
    Lock
        <Lock checked later>
    Hold released
        <Release checked elsewhere>
can't happen
    Door opened
        <Already open> The door is already open.
    Door closed
        <Open cannot instantly close> The door is open and cannot instantaneously be closed.
    Door blocked
        <Blocking makes no sense when open> Makes no sense if the door is open.
    Unlock
        <Cabin not moving>
--
state Cancel open delay
activity
    Time to close ->* me
    Open delay canceled -> me
transitions
    Open delay canceled > HOLDING OPEN
--
state HOLDING OPEN
activity
    !Held ? Hold released -> me
transitions
    Hold released > CLOSING
ignore
    Passenger open
        <Already open so ignored>
    Passenger close
        Passenger is simultaneously requesting hold open and close. Open overrides,
        so we just ignore.
    Lock
        <Lock checked later>
can't happen
    Door opened
        <Already open>
    Door closed
        <Open cannot instantly close>
    Door blocked
        <Blocking makes no sense when open>
    Unlock
        <Cabin not moving>
    Time to close
        <Delay always canceled>
--
state CLOSING
activity
transitions
    Door closed > CLOSED
    Passenger open > OPENING
    Door blocked > Count block
ignore
    Passenger close
        We’re already closing, so just ignore.
    Lock
        <Lock checked later>
    Hold released
        <Release checked elsewhere>
can't happen
    Door opened
        If we are closing, there’s no way to become open.
    Unlock
        <Cabin not moving>
    Time to close
        <Delay always canceled>
--
state CLOSED
activity
    Close attempts.reset
    Blocked.unset
    Lock requested? Lock -> me
    // May be None
    Door closed -> /R4/R53/Transfer
transitions
    Lock > LOCKED
    Passenger open > OPENING
ignore
    Passenger close
        <Already closed so ignored> The door is already closed, so just ignore.
    Hold released
        <Release checked elsewhere>
can't happen
    Door opened
        The door is closed and cannot instantaneously be open.
    Door closed
        <Already closed> The door is already closed.
    Door blocked
        <Closed door cannot be blocked> You can’t block a closed door.
    Unlock
        Cabin can’t send an unlock before a lock, which would have put us in the LOCKED state.
    Time to close
        <Delay always canceled>
--
state LOCKED
activity
    // Tell the cabin that we’re ready to go
    Lock requested.unset
    Doors secure -> /R4/Cabin
transitions
    Unlock > OPENING
ignore
    Passenger open
        The door is not safe to open in this state so the request is ignored.
    Passenger close
        <Already closed so ignored>
    Hold released
        <Release checked elsewhere>
can't happen
    Door opened
        The whole point of this state is to ensure the door is not opened.
        It cannot open while locked.
    Door closed
        <Already closed>
    Door blocked
        <Closed door cannot be blocked>
    Lock
        The cabin is synched so that it won’t issue another lock request before unlocking.
    Time to close
        <Delay always canceled>
--
state Count block
activity
    Close attempts.increment
    (Close attempts > /R4/R2/Bank.Max close attempts) ? Cannot close door -> me : {
        Blocked.set
        Keep trying -> me
    }
transitions
    Keep trying > OPENING
    Cannot close door > CANNOT CLOSE
--
state CANNOT CLOSE
activity
    Take out of service -> /R4/Cabin
ignore
    Hold released
        <Release checked elsewhere>
can't happen
    Door opened
        <Shaft out of service> Presumably the shaft is out of service and no events will be
        issued until it is back in service again.
    Door closed
        <Shaft out of service>
    Door blocked
        <Shaft out of service>
    Passenger open
        <Shaft out of service>
    Passenger close
        <Shaft out of service>
    Lock
        <Shaft out of service>
    Unlock
        <Shaft out of service>
    Time to close
        <Delay always canceled>
--